  "policy": "Copied per-pixel-guarded primary 8192-sample policy versus exact current baseline on first-party deterministic derivatives of the pinned original screenshot: the entire screenshot transposed to portrait and a wide screenshot with sparse zero-alpha pixels on its final row retaining original hidden RGB. Report any growth rather than hide it. Verify every original native/Rust and public sample with complete nonduplicate coverage, actual final grouping/DC/reference frames, unchanged inputs and owned closure. The already encoded ordinary-frame guard uses one half bit per pixel, independent of RGB/RGBA channel count, and skips very cheap inputs; it is a heuristic, not a universal no-growth proof. Fresh guarded-policy pair overhead and original-limit qualification remain separate; no production adoption or overall parity claim."
